---
import Brutal from '../layouts/Brutal.astro';
import { meta, slots, REPO } from '../lib/data.js';
const count = (v) => slots.filter((s) => s.verify?.verdict === v).length;
---
<Brutal title="Method" description="How Founder Studio picks were researched, verified and consolidated, and what is still unverified.">
  <div class="wrap page">
    <header class="ph">
      <h1 class="display">Method</h1>
      <div><p>How every pick was made, how it was checked, and what is still open.</p><span class="cap">Checked {meta.built}</span></div>
    </header>

    <div class="tally">
      <div><b>{count('ok')}</b><span class="cap">Confirmed</span></div>
      <div><b>{count('fixed')}</b><span class="cap">Corrected</span></div>
      <div><b>{count('doubt')}</b><span class="cap">In doubt</span></div>
      <div><b>{count('stale')}</b><span class="cap">Stale</span></div>
    </div>

    <div class="essay">
      <h2>Who</h2>
      <div><p>Solo founders and small teams building AI products, on any OS, any budget and in any country. The site assumes nothing about the subscriptions, hardware or location you already have. One opinion is stated openly: we recommend Claude Code as the coding agent, so its ecosystem gets its own track.</p></div>
      <h2>Research</h2>
      <div><p>Thirteen tracks were researched in six parallel passes. For each slot, at least four credible options were compared on capability, maturity, maintenance, developer experience, price-to-value, lock-in and licence. The best overall became the pick, whatever it costs. When it isn't free, the best free option with real commercial terms is named beside it. Where the answer changes by country or OS, a short note says how.</p></div>
      <h2>Verify</h2>
      <div><p>Four independent verifiers re-opened every pick's source and checked fees, limits, dates, acquisitions, shutdowns and legal claims against primary sources. Each tool page shows its stamp and the verifier's note.</p></div>
      <h2>Decide</h2>
      <div><p>Where tracks overlapped, one call was made so the stack fits together. See <a href="/decisions/">Decisions</a>.</p></div>
      <h2>Limits</h2>
      <div><p>Prices and free tiers change monthly, so check before you pay. Tax and legal content is research, not advice: confirm it with an accountant or a lawyer in your country.</p></div>
      <h2>Use it</h2>
      <div><p>Load the same data into Claude Code with the <a href="/skills/">Founder Studio skills</a>: ask for a tool, or get a stack picked for your project.</p></div>
      <h2>Fix it</h2>
      <div><p>Every tool page links to its data file on <a href={REPO}>GitHub</a>. Pull requests that include a source link are welcome.</p></div>
    </div>

    <section class="block">
      <div class="block-h"><h2>Open questions</h2><span class="cap">{meta.unverified.length} not yet confirmed</span></div>
      <ol class="qs">{meta.unverified.map((u) => <li>{u}</li>)}</ol>
    </section>
  </div>
</Brutal>
